1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,880
A solar certificate is only worth something if it

2
00:00:02,890 --> 00:00:03,620
can be used once.

3
00:00:03,630 --> 00:00:06,160
Today the burn lives in one system and the

4
00:00:06,170 --> 00:00:07,510
public record in another.

5
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:09,530
They can disagree.

6
00:00:15,230 --> 00:00:17,900
This is Mentari on the QoreChain testnet.

7
00:00:17,910 --> 00:00:19,360
I press Retire now.

8
00:00:19,370 --> 00:00:23,500
One transaction burns five hundred watt-hours in an EVM

9
00:00:23,510 --> 00:00:26,650
contract and writes a receipt into the Native receipts

10
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:28,900
book through the Cross-VM bridge.

11
00:00:28,910 --> 00:00:30,410
Both ledgers go up by one.

12
00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:33,930
The explorer shows it signed with ML-DSA-87.

13
00:00:42,230 --> 00:00:42,890
Now I make it fail.

14
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:45,390
This button writes the Native receipt,

15
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:46,620
then reverts on the EVM side.

16
00:00:46,630 --> 00:00:48,180
The receipt count does not move.

17
00:00:48,190 --> 00:00:50,030
The chain undid the Native write.

18
00:00:50,040 --> 00:00:52,440
The other two buttons fail on the Native side

19
00:00:52,450 --> 00:00:54,530
and at the bridge allowlist.

20
00:01:03,030 --> 00:01:04,580
Anyone can check a retirement.

21
00:01:04,590 --> 00:01:05,720
The page reads both records.

22
00:01:05,730 --> 00:01:07,200
Each one names the other,

23
00:01:07,210 --> 00:01:09,230
and the Mentari contract wrote the receipt.

24
00:01:09,240 --> 00:01:12,690
Then your browser checks the meter signatures again.

25
00:01:19,390 --> 00:01:23,300
Certificates are minted from meter readings signed with ML-DSA-87.

26
00:01:23,310 --> 00:01:27,300
The contract checks each signature with the pqcVerify precompile.

27
00:01:27,310 --> 00:01:31,280
A reading signed with another key mints nothing.

28
00:01:31,290 --> 00:01:35,270
A classical key alone cannot retire: the chain refuses

29
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:35,880
it.

30
00:01:42,950 --> 00:01:43,730
One thing I did not expect.

31
00:01:43,740 --> 00:01:47,120
The docs mark calls from a Native account into

32
00:01:47,130 --> 00:01:48,260
the EVM as not yet tested.

33
00:01:48,270 --> 00:01:48,870
I ran it.

34
00:01:48,690 --> 00:01:51,450
One hybrid-signed transaction,

35
00:01:51,460 --> 00:01:52,430
with no EVM window open,

36
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:55,310
ran the contract and wrote the receipt back on

37
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:56,190
the Native side.

38
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:58,610
Retire now uses that route.

39
00:02:06,510 --> 00:02:07,750
You do not have to trust this video.

40
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:09,740
Clone the repo and run pnpm demo.

41
00:02:09,750 --> 00:02:10,350
It needs no key.

42
00:02:10,290 --> 00:02:14,400
It checks every retirement and every recorded case again

43
00:02:14,410 --> 00:02:16,730
from public endpoints.

44
00:02:23,830 --> 00:02:25,480
The meters are simulated.

45
00:02:25,490 --> 00:02:27,620
The signatures and the chain are real.

46
00:02:27,630 --> 00:02:30,280
I built Mentari on my own in Malaysia with

47
00:02:30,290 --> 00:02:31,580
AI coding agents.

48
00:02:31,590 --> 00:02:34,130
This voice is an AI clone of my own.

